  6071  /**
  6072   * g_variant_byteswap:
  6073   * @value: a #GVariant
  6074   *
  6075   * Performs a byteswapping operation on the contents of @value.  The
  6076   * result is that all multi-byte numeric data contained in @value is
  6077   * byteswapped.  That includes 16, 32, and 64bit signed and unsigned
  6078   * integers as well as file handles and double precision floating point
  6079   * values.
  6080   *
  6081   * This function is an identity mapping on any value that does not
  6082   * contain multi-byte numeric data.  That include strings, booleans,
  6083   * bytes and containers containing only these things (recursively).
  6084   *
  6085   * While this function can safely handle untrusted, non-normal data, it is
  6086   * recommended to check whether the input is in normal form beforehand, using
  6087   * g_variant_is_normal_form(), and to reject non-normal inputs if your
  6088   * application can be strict about what inputs it rejects.
  6089   *
  6090   * The returned value is always in normal form and is marked as trusted.
  6091   * A full, not floating, reference is returned.
  6092   *
  6093   * Returns: (transfer full): the byteswapped form of @value
  6094   *
